# Snappy bar (locked 2026-11-03, live `51e8b9a`)

Owner baseline after worker refinements. Future audits **compare to these numbers**. A regression vs this bar is a bug even if a feature is “correct.”

Measured gzip, Asia edge `hkg1` → Railway origin, quiet warm (not a sequential storm). Floor ~250ms is RTT, not GIL.

| Surface | Bar |
|---|---|
| `/health` | ~0.28–0.33s · ready · RSS ~0.95GB idle · alert quiet |
| Browse `/api/characters` `/api/units` | ~0.28–0.31s |
| Char / unit detail | ~0.26–0.31s |
| BSP Top 10 warm + 304 | ~0.27–0.29s |
| `/api/banner_timeline` | ~0.28s |
| Banner votes | ~0.30s · `private, max-age=15` |
| SPI `/api/sp_investment` | ~0.38s · ~726KB gzip |
| `/api/whats_new` warm + 304 | ~0.25–0.29s · `public, max-age=300` |
| `/api/tag_matrix` | ~0.4–0.5s |
| 12× parallel char details | wall ~0.66s |
| Adaptive band at idle | **calm** (pair cache near 6k ceiling) |

## What “worse” means

- `/health` or warm detail/browse/`/tl`/`/new`/BSP climbing past **~0.5s** while idle
- SPI warm past **~0.8s**
- Band stuck on **pressure** at RSS &lt; ~1.1GB and rpm &lt; 80
- Parallel detail wall multi-second (queue saturation)

Do not “fix” the ~250ms RTT floor with extra workers, boot-prewarm of multi‑MB boards, or rate limits. See `live-perf-never-break-snappy.mdc`.
